= Dangling references, orphans and inconsistent edges =

**Dangling references:** none found in the Kinnect Foundation or Specification. Every cited SA, ST, PS, HV, VT, HFC, M, EM, TECH, DS, HP, RP, OBJ, UC, Premise, Claim, TDP, IDP and AT-01 resolves to a defined entry.

**Orphans:** no selected Foundation entity is wholly disconnected. TECH-02 and TECH-07 to TECH-09 have no outgoing Specification edges because they are explicitly rejected alternatives, not accidental omissions.

Two one-sided edges were found while compiling this page and corrected at their source:

|=Edge|=Missing from|=Correction
|HV-04 operationalized-by M-19|M-19 on b4.1|M-19 now names both HV-04 Safety and HV-05 Well-being.
|VT-05 strained-by TECH-18|TECH-18 on c1.1|TECH-18 now names VT-05, matching the tension page and its privacy/identity drawback.

= Open tensions =

No tension has been empirically resolved. “Provisionally resolved” means the specification contains a defensible design stance and a Premise/Claim intended to test it; it does not mean Evidence exists.

|=Tension|=Recorded status|=Design stance pending evidence|=Checked by
|VT-01 Privacy vs Social connectedness|Provisionally resolved|Profile items remain private by default; each disclosure is separately released; matching and introduction use only mutually released details.|UC02-F2-PR2, UC02-F2-CL4; M-01, M-09, M-10
|VT-02 Social connectedness vs Autonomy|Open|Kinnect may propose, but each resident is asked privately and independently; refusal is ordinary, final and not disclosed to the other resident.|UC02-F1-PR1, UC02-F1-CL3; M-01, M-07, M-09
|VT-03 Truthfulness vs Well-being|Provisionally resolved|Kinnect does not confirm a false premise or deliver painful truths. It gives a truthful boundary and hands the question to a named trusted person.|UC01-F4-PR4, UC01-F4-CL8; M-01, M-09, M-10
|VT-04 Dignity vs Social connectedness|Open|Introduce symmetrically, repeat both names without exposing who forgot, offer one shared-ground statement, then step back.|UC02-F3-PR3, UC01-F3-CL5; M-01, M-07, M-09
|VT-05 Privacy vs Identity|Open|Profiles preserve meaningful biography but each item is private until released. Raw audio and transcripts are not retained; TECH-18 remains only envisioned.|UC02-F6-PR6, UC02-F2-CL4; M-01, M-09, M-10
|VT-06 Privacy and Autonomy vs Well-being|Open|Room-presence notes are opt-in and coarse, used to offer contact rather than compel it; continuous tracking is rejected.|UC03-F5-PR5, UC03-F5-CL7; M-01, M-09, M-22

= Completeness check =

== Required checks ==

|=Check|=Result|=Stance
|Situated Activity without a Goal|None. SA-01 to SA-04 each state a Goal.|No action.
|Human Value without recognition criteria|None. HV-01 to HV-08 each state served and violated criteria.|No action.
|Human Factors Concept without an associated Measure|None. HFC-01 to HFC-08 and HFC-15 to HFC-17 each name at least one Measure.|No action.
|Selected Technology Option addressing nothing|None. TECH-01 and TECH-03 to TECH-06 address at least one Human Value. TECH-18 also addresses HV-03, but remains envisioned.|Rejected options remain as documented alternatives without forward Specification edges.
|Premise without an operational Measure|None. M-01 covers all six Premises; M-10 additionally covers PR2 and PR4.|Evidence still requires EM-01 to run.
|Current Claim without an operational Measure|None. CL1 to CL9 each has at least one Measure through M-02 to M-10.|No Claim has Evidence yet.

== Remaining gaps ==

|=Gap|=Stance
|ST-05 Activity coordinator is marked Direct but has no Human Persona.|Add a persona or explicitly justify treating ST-05 through role requirements rather than a Persona. The current three Personas cover residents and the care worker only.
|ER-03's composite primary hypothesis and first-time-usability hypothesis have no final Claim IDs.|Resolve before the study runs. Either narrow the hypotheses to existing Claims or add explicit Claims, then replace the provisional targets on M-19 to M-23 and EM-08.
|AT-01 Build 1 (##sce-poc##) is a formative web simulation using cloud STT/TTS and a hosted LLM (PR6 fails by design; F5 not yet implemented).|Documented on AT-01. Complete Build 2 (local speech/prepared lines + F5 follow-up) to pass EM-01 before resident contact, and Build 3 (**Pepper+** with simultaneous speaking/listening support and TECH-18 hardware acceleration) before running ER-03.
|TECH-18 (**Pepper+**) is envisioned for AT-01 Build 3 but not physically built.|Until it exists, M-21 and the free-conversation parts of ER-03 cannot run on physical hardware under the stated no-cloud policy.
|ER-03 uses one care home per arm.|Site effects cannot be separated from the intervention effect. Baseline adjustment does not remove this limitation.
|ER-03 proposes proximity badges although TECH-09 rejects wearable location sensing.|Resolve whether time-limited, separately consented room-level sensing is acceptable or replace it with the coarser TECH-03 approach.
|No Kinnect Evaluation Report has results and no Kinnect Evidence page exists.|Keep all Foundation claims provisional until the artifact exists and EM-01 to EM-04 or EM-08 have actually run.
|Thresholds and operating rules in O-2 to O-9 remain open.|Set them through the EM-01 pilot, site checks, legal review and decisions with residents and care staff.

= Status of these edges =

The chain is conceptually complete from situated activities through values, human factors, measures, technology and the current Specification. It supports a project about consent-gated social introductions and renewed peer contact; walking is only one optional activity selected from both residents' preferences. The chain remains a design hypothesis: AT-01 Build 1 (##sce-poc##) is implemented for formative evaluation, while AT-01 Builds 2–3 (Pepper+ / TECH-18) and the evaluations are not yet complete, and no empirical Evidence is claimed.
